{title: Sing For Joy}
{subtitle: Psalms 95:1–2}
{key: D}
{tempo: 83}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [D] | [Dmaj7] | [G] [A7/G] | [D] [Dmaj7] |
| [G] [A7/G] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]Come let us [Dmaj7]sing for [G]joy to the [A]Lord
Let us [Bm7]shout a[A]loud to our [G]rock [A7/G]
[D]He is the [Dmaj7]source of [G]our salva[A]tion
The foun[Bm7]dation of [A]our [D]hope
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Let us [G]come before [A]him with thanks[D]giving
Shout to [G]him with [A]songs of [Bm7]praise
For the [G]Lord is a great [A]God
A [D]great [A/C#]King a[Bm7]bove all [A][G]gods [A]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]In his [Dmaj7]hand are the [G]depths of the [A]earth
And the [Bm7]heights of the [A]mountains are [G]his
[D]The sea [Dmaj7]is his [G]for he made [A]it
[Bm7]His hands formed [A]the dry [D]land
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[D]Come let us sing [Dmaj7]for joy [G]to the Lord
Shout [A]aloud to [Bm7]the rock of our [A]salvation
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Let [G]us come before him with thanks[A]giving
Shout to [D]him with songs of [G]praise
For [A]the Lord [Bm7]is a great [G]God
A great King [A]above all [D]gods
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[A/C#]Shout to [Bm7]him with [A]songs of [G]praise
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
| [A] | [D] [Dmaj7] | [G] [A] | [D] [Dmaj7] |
| [G] [A] | [A] |
